  "instructions": [
    "Heat the oven to 425 F. Line a rimmed baking sheet with parchment paper.",
    "In a large bowl, combine the turkey, breadcrumbs, parmesan, egg, garlic, oregano, 3/4 tsp salt, and pepper. Mix gently with your hands until just combined.",
    "Roll the mixture into 20 meatballs, about 1 1/2 inches wide. Place them on the baking sheet.",
    "Bake for 16 to 18 minutes, until browned and an instant-read thermometer inserted in the center reads 165 F.",
    "While the meatballs bake, bring the water and 1 tbsp salt to a boil in a large pot. Cook the spaghetti for 9 to 10 minutes, until tender, then drain.",
    "Warm the marinara in a large saucepan over medium heat for 5 minutes, until steaming.",
    "Add the baked meatballs to the sauce and stir gently to coat. Simmer for 2 minutes.",
    "Divide the spaghetti among four plates and top with the meatballs and sauce. Cool leftovers before freezing in airtight containers."
  ],
